Subject: [PATCH 24/24] The packets become one entry with children, not a
 chapter each; the weed quote moves to where it is answered
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two navigation problems, one cause. The sidebar is a curated reading order of ten
entries, and the criminal packet took one of them; on the same pattern the five lanes
would have taken five, and the reading order would have become a directory listing of
packets with the argument buried under them.

So the packets nest. "The packets" is renamed **The review packets**, carries the index
page, and every lane packet hangs beneath it as a child — a fifth lane now costs a
click, not a chapter. The sidebar returns to nine top-level entries and the remaining
orders close up behind it. Children are matched to the parent by its exact title, so
the title in _config.yml and the parent key must stay in step; the comment above the
block says so.

The front page: the Ball quote — "yes, we accidentally made a weed" — was the third
thing on the page, above the record, doing rhetorical work before the reader had been
told what the Act is. It moves down into "Can a model act?", which is the section that
answers it: the emergent-ecology framing and the salmonella paragraph now sit directly
under the paragraph about acts having actors, where the quote is evidence rather than
an opening flourish. The dated record keeps its 8 August row, so the quote is still on
the page twice — once as a date, once as an argument — and neither copy is the top of
the page.
